---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy | Bigby.cloud" description="Bigby.cloud's privacy policy.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="py-5">
      <div class="container" style="max-width: 720px;">

      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

      <p>
            Bigby.cloud Ltd<br>
            71-75 Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London, United Kingdom, WC2H 9JQ<br>
            Email: support@bigby.cloud<br>
            Company number: 17214602<br>
            ICO registration reference: ZC235231<br>
            Last updated: 11 September 2026
        </p>

      <p>We provide a cloud file storage and office suite. This notice explains how we use your personal data when you sign up for and use our service.</p>

      <h2>What data we collect</h2>
      <ul>
          <li><strong>Account data</strong>: Name, email address, billing details, company name.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage data</strong>: IP address, browser type, device identifiers, timestamps, access logs, error logs.</li>
          <li><strong>Support data</strong>: Anything you send us when you contact support, including email address.</li>
          <li><strong>Optional analytics</strong>: We may use analytics tools to understand how the service is used (we will update this list with more details at a later date).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we use it and the legal basis</h2>
      <table class="table">
          <tr>
              <th>Purpose</th>
              <th>Legal basis</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
              <td>Running your account, billing, and providing the service</td>
              <td>Contract (we need this to give you the service)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
              <td>Keeping the service secure, preventing fraud, and debugging</td>
              <td>Legitimate interest (recognised under UK data protection law)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
              <td>Sending service updates or important security notices</td>
              <td>Contract or legitimate interest</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
              <td>Marketing emails (if any)</td>
              <td>Contract or legitimate interest (we require you to receive emails from us for new features, products, or similar during the alpha testing period to ensure our alpha testers are actively participating in tests. After this, you may opt out entirely.)</td>
          </tr>
      </table>

      <p>We do not make automated decisions about you that have legal or significant effects.</p>

      <h2>Who sees your data</h2>
      <p>Our staff and the following sub-processors who help run the service:</p>
      <ul>
          <li><strong>OVH</strong> (hosting infrastructure)</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (security and CDN)</li>
          <li><strong>AWS</strong> (email, backup, and auxiliary services)</li>
          <li><strong>Grafana</strong> (log collection, metrics collection, and monitoring)</li>
          <li><strong>Formspree</strong> (website forms)</li>
          <li><strong>Infomaniak</strong> (email and support requests)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Your uploaded files and documents stay in the <strong>UK</strong>. However, some account data (such as emails for authentication or support) may be processed in the <strong>EU</strong> by our sub-processors. The UK government has decided that EU data protection law is adequate for these transfers, so your data is safeguarded by that adequacy decision.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>We keep your account data for <strong>up to 60 days</strong> after you close your account or we terminate it, then we delete it. We may delete your data between 0 and 60 days from the date your account is closed or terminated.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can:</p>
      <ul>
          <li>Ask what data we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Ask us to correct, delete, or restrict the use of your data.</li>
          <li>Object to how we use your data.</li>
          <li>Ask for a copy of your data.</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent at any time (this does not affect past processing).</li>
      </ul>

      <p>To exercise any of these rights, email us at support@bigby.cloud. We will acknowledge your request within <strong>30 days</strong> and respond properly without undue delay.</p>

      <p>If you are unhappy with how we use your data, you have the right to complain to the <strong>Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</strong>.</p>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
